{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question","id":287798,"title":"On odd RP question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-20T10:24:06-07:00","id":287798,"title":"On odd RP question","content":"I'm playing a mixed template game where I'm playing as a male Mage that is about to go out on a date with a female Werewolf Alpha. After having a temporary bout of Narcissistic God Complex from a spell that went horribly wrong, she grabbed him and made out with him in order to get him to stop recklessly attacking a monster of unknown power; afterwards they both admitted that they liked it and he apologized for his behavior when he sobered up. I know that the Werewolf player is partially amused, partially toying with making my character uncomfortable as payback for him being a jerk the other night. <br /> <br /> What social snafoos should a mage character be wary of when dating a werewolf? Is this a pairing that anyone else has had shipped before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:39:50-07:00","id":287829,"title":"","content":"Depending on their tribe, they have different vows they have to abide by. Fire-Touched don't like being lied to and for the Storm Lords, it's 'Allow no one to witness or tend to your weakness.' So getting intimate with one can be awkward depending upon their views of weakness.<br /> <br /> Plus there's the whole Death Rage thing. Betrayal by loved ones is something that can bring it out in werewolves of any Harmony.<br /> <br /> Silver's a big no no, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:40:45-07:00","id":287831,"title":"","content":"Does the mage in question have any understanding of the Spirit Arcanum? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As far as socializing, I'd say follow the werewolf's lead if you're going to spend a lot of time in her territory, or potentially around other Uratha. It's not only safer (probably), it's just polite! Also, try to avoid falling into the magely trap of assuming you know more than the other supernatural in the room.<br /> <br /> Beyond that... how's your Composure rating? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T11:02:25-07:00","id":287836,"title":"","content":"Our ST isn't applying Lunacy to mages I believe but my composure is 4 and I can bring up a 4 dot mental shield. I don't have any dots in spirit but my character is also a reasonably liberal hunter in that he hangs out with other hunters that focus less on the &quot;shoot on sight&quot; mentality and more on the &quot;find the monsters that are actually killing people&quot; point of view. Through his time hunting malicious spirits on occasion, he knows more about the subject than the average non-spirit mage. I have silver bullets on me usually but I'll leave them at home...<br /> <br /> Especially because the date itself is a way of making up for his asshatery the other night while he was struck with narcissism, my mage is fully willing to follow her lead, although in normal circumstances they will probably butt heads. Part of the reason this whole thing started out is the Promethean in the group started teasing both of us saying our arguments and fights look awfully close to flirting. We are the two most alpha personalities in the game (me because I'm a time/mind mage that keeps the city safe and usually thinks that everyone else is way too naiive and reckless; her because she is an <i>actual</i> werewolf alpha). Our similar personalities seem to be what are drawing our characters together but at the same time it could lead to some terrifying fights in the future too...<br /> <br /> As for her tribe, I'm not sure. I know she is Forsaken and I think she is a Boneshadow of the New Moon. For death rage, I know for a fact that some of my hanging time spells when activated will let me easily outrun her and dodge like a pro. Plus Telepathic Control and Emotional Urging: Calm should help a bit. Still, I don't want to take any chances though...Gourou is scary stuff!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hope the clarifying information can better help viewers to give accurate advice for the situation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","user":"Cardran","date":". 10-20-2014, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T05:26:53-07:00","id":288462,"title":"","content":"I think social awareness will be much more important than sheet stats for a successful rp. You mentioned the key fact already: she is her pack's alpha. Be worthy of her taking the lead - follow respectfully, but make sure you keep up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:30:54-07:00","id":288521,"title":"","content":"Honestly, your concerns are going to be amazingly individual.<br /> <br /> Keep an escape option ready at all time, work on that composure, and for God's sake, don't piss off the totem or pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:45:54-07:00","id":288531,"title":"","content":"Acamoths? No problem, dealt with them before.<br /> <br /> Seers of the Throne? Yeah, no worries.<br /> <br /> Broken-hearted Uratha with a strongly bonded pack who are now all just as upset as she is.....................<b>run, just <i>fucking <span style=\"font-size:14px\">run</span>!!!!</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:29:41-07:00","id":288553,"title":"","content":"No kidding.<br /> <br /> Just watch the ego bouncing and you should be safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T08:28:08-07:00","id":289619,"title":"","content":"Some great quotes in response to my question. Papa Bear especially gave me a chuckle. The date scene went really well until her pack member showed up after spying on us and freaked out saying that, &quot;He's a hunter! When he gets mad at you later he'll kill both of us! It's what he does!&quot; She ran off after the Alpha got mad at her but that became a whole drama laced thing. The drama was then made worse because one of the female Mage PCs was apparently crushing on the Alpha pretty hard. I maintain that the drama is not my character's fault, the alpha pursued him, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T05:45:14-07:00","id":290454,"title":"","content":"I was really hoping it would go well for you, but at the same time... imagining both a mage and a werewolf on their separate couches, in fuzzy slippers and bathrobes, sobbing about how 'they don't understand me' while eating out of gallons of ice cream... It was, how shall I say, a win-win for me, whatever the outcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:39:17-07:00","id":293896,"title":"","content":"No, we instead get to deal with other dysfunctional issues. She wants to resolve disagreements with my character by treating him like a pack member, i.e. yelling at him angrily to do whatever she says no matter how irrational. At some point our very strong willed characters will probably end up having a shouting match that escalates to her shifting into either Dalu or Urshul form while swearing at me in Spirit Tongue (one of the only languages my level of mind magic <i>can't</i> understand), while I in turn do an intentional Nimus flare while swearing at her in Atlantean High Speech. This entertaining image will likely eventually be ended when either she storms off or I cast a mind spell on her which is the equivalent of the &quot;Point of View Gun&quot; from the Hitch Hiker's Guide to the Galaxy movie....or she'll rip my throat out in Gauru form. You know, whichever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T07:36:06-07:00","id":294801,"title":"","content":"But making up will certainly be fun... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T12:29:19-07:00","id":295069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=293896#post293896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we instead get to deal with other dysfunctional issues. She wants to resolve disagreements with my character by treating him like a pack member, i.e. yelling at him angrily to do whatever she says no matter how irrational. At some point our very strong willed characters will probably end up having a shouting match that escalates to her shifting into either Dalu or Urshul form while swearing at me in Spirit Tongue (one of the only languages my level of mind magic <i>can't</i> understand), while I in turn do an intentional Nimus flare while swearing at her in Atlantean High Speech. This entertaining image will likely eventually be ended when either she storms off or I cast a mind spell on her which is the equivalent of the &quot;Point of View Gun&quot; from the Hitch Hiker's Guide to the Galaxy movie....or she'll rip my throat out in Gauru form. You know, whichever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like my kind of woman..............in fact, I married one like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:43:56-07:00","id":295163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=295069#post295069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like my kind of woman..............in fact, I married one like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You married blood thirsty monsterous she-wolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:50:27-07:00","id":295171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=295163#post295163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You married blood thirsty monsterous she-wolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty close, yeah. I know it's cross-species, but I'd be bored with anything less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T19:58:31-07:00","id":295553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=293896#post293896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we instead get to deal with other dysfunctional issues. She wants to resolve disagreements with my character by treating him like a pack member, i.e. yelling at him angrily to do whatever she says no matter how irrational. At some point our very strong willed characters will probably end up having a shouting match that escalates to her shifting into either Dalu or Urshul form while swearing at me in Spirit Tongue (one of the only languages my level of mind magic <i>can't</i> understand), while I in turn do an intentional Nimus flare while swearing at her in Atlantean High Speech. This entertaining image will likely eventually be ended when either she storms off or I cast a mind spell on her which is the equivalent of the &quot;Point of View Gun&quot; from the Hitch Hiker's Guide to the Galaxy movie....or she'll rip my throat out in Gauru form. You know, whichever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jumping into this conversation perhaps a bit late, I personally would not use any mind spell on her in the event that she goes ballistic. She is a dominant alpha, you are sheeple (even if you are an enlightened one). Just accept that fact, say &quot;yes dear&quot; and take over the beta position within the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T07:31:01-07:00","id":295838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=295553#post295553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jumping into this conversation perhaps a bit late, I personally would not use any mind spell on her in the event that she goes ballistic. She is a dominant alpha, you are sheeple (even if you are an enlightened one). Just accept that fact, say &quot;yes dear&quot; and take over the beta position within the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages do often tend to forget that, don't they? And it comes as quite a shock when they are forcibly reminded of that fact. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T08:01:55-07:00","id":295861,"title":"","content":"Hooray dramatic/belligerent-sexual tension!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T08:34:07-07:00","id":295885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=295553#post295553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jumping into this conversation perhaps a bit late, I personally would not use any mind spell on her in the event that she goes ballistic. She is a dominant alpha, you are sheeple (even if you are an enlightened one). Just accept that fact, say &quot;yes dear&quot; and take over the beta position within the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It figures that on the Werewolf board I'd be told to be the beta. I wonder if I would get the same response from the Mage board :/? <br /> <br /> At the moment she has agreed to minimize the irrational demands for submission if my character makes an earnest effort to cut down on his alcoholism. I think my PC got the worse end of this deal considering his vice is gluttony and he drinks about as much as one would expect from a jaded Time mage/hunter (his flask is almost as important as his gun!). Robbed of my PC's flask, now I have to figure out something else to pantomime whenever something horrifying or stupid irritates my PC...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T12:54:10-07:00","id":296080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=295885#post295885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It figures that on the Werewolf board I'd be told to be the beta. I wonder if I would get the same response from the Mage board :/?<br /> <br /> At the moment she has agreed to minimize the irrational demands for submission if my character makes an earnest effort to cut down on his alcoholism. I think my PC got the worse end of this deal considering his vice is gluttony and he drinks about as much as one would expect from a jaded Time mage/hunter (his flask is almost as important as his gun!). Robbed of my PC's flask, now I have to figure out something else to pantomime whenever something horrifying or stupid irritates my PC...</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep the pantomime, only now it's being done IN and out of character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T14:18:24-07:00","id":296166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=296080#post296080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep the pantomime, only now it's being done IN and out of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Instead of Phantom Limb, I have Phantom Flask syndrome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T15:11:40-07:00","id":296224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=295885#post295885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It figures that on the Werewolf board I'd be told to be the beta. I wonder if I would get the same response from the Mage board :/?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would other Mages have any say in what is going on with your character in this particular situation? Also, I can't really see any role-play reason why they would deny it either since you could always argue you are pursuing knowledge wherever it presents itself which Mages in general love to hear.<br /> <br /> Take a dot or two in spirit arcana, become best pals with the totem, and stay the hell out of the shadow unless you want to start suffering adverse effects such as seen in Book of Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T16:13:25-07:00","id":296250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=296224#post296224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would other Mages have any say in what is going on with your character in this particular situation? Also, I can't really see any role-play reason why they would deny it either since you could always argue you are pursuing knowledge wherever it presents itself which Mages in general love to hear.<br /> <br /> Take a dot or two in spirit arcana, become best pals with the totem, and stay the hell out of the shadow unless you want to start suffering adverse effects such as seen in Book of Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding the part where Cardran means inquiry on the Awakening boards regarding the same thing...<br /> <br /> If this pack allows such a thing as having an alpha be bewitched (really or not) to the point the ruling alpha would conceive having a human occupy the role of Beta; or having their totem be exposed to a mage they deserve to have elders berate them for their cattle like innocence. There should, at the very least, be stories told about how mages have been observed making pack totems their literal bitches.<br /> <br /> When they didn't outright replaced the spirit with a simulacrum that reported back to the mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 10-29-2014, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T18:51:02-07:00","id":296374,"title":"","content":"Ephsy is correct, I was joking about posting the same question on the mage board although I must say that the answers from the WtF board have been extremely entertaining thus far. I had to placate the junior Werewolf of the pack by entering a Changeling pledge stating that &quot;I won't harm either of them unless they are going to imminently cause harm to either myself or an innocent.&quot; Prior to that, the junior wolf was convinced that I would flip out and shoot both of them the moment we got into a lover's spat because &quot;he's a hunter.&quot; Hey, my mage is a <i>very </i>progressive hunter, no hunting unless they are actually hurting people. As a mage, I'd be monstrously hypocritical otherwise.<br /> <br /> My character decided to one-up his Werewolf date. For the second date he called in a favor from a local space master in order to get an all expense paid round trip portal to Italy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T22:33:20-07:00","id":296596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=296374#post296374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephsy is correct, I was joking about posting the same question on the mage board although I must say that the answers from the WtF board have been extremely entertaining thus far. I had to placate the junior Werewolf of the pack by entering a Changeling pledge stating that &quot;I won't harm either of them unless they are going to imminently cause harm to either myself or an innocent.&quot; Prior to that, the junior wolf was convinced that I would flip out and shoot both of them the moment we got into a lover's spat because &quot;he's a hunter.&quot; Hey, my mage is a <i>very </i>progressive hunter, no hunting unless they are actually hurting people. As a mage, I'd be monstrously hypocritical otherwise.<br /> <br /> My character decided to one-up his Werewolf date. For the second date he called in a favor from a local space master in order to get an all expense paid round trip portal to Italy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why things between Uratha and mages wouldn't work: Uratha are predators. Take an otherwise innocent lawyer, who's pretty good at his job, and has basically turned the local precinct into a revolving door. (&quot;Better Call Saul!&quot; anyone?) A pack could deem that this guy has tipped the turf's balance, and it's preventing them from shaping their territory as they'd prefer. Ergo, they'd whack the lawyer. Literally make him disappear (decaying dusts are handy).<br /> <br /> Also, props for the most banal favor you could ask from a Master that I've ever seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T22:37:17-07:00","id":296600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=296596#post296596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why things between Uratha and mages wouldn't work: Uratha are predators. Take an otherwise innocent lawyer, who's pretty good at his job, and has basically turned the local precinct into a revolving door. (&quot;Better Call Saul!&quot; anyone?) A pack could deem that this guy has tipped the turf's balance, and it's preventing them from shaping their territory as they'd prefer. Ergo, they'd whack the lawyer. Literally make him disappear (decaying dusts are handy).<br /> <br /> Also, props for the most banal favor you could ask from a Master that I've ever seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part of the story is supposed to have elements of a rom-com, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T08:01:31-07:00","id":297116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=296600#post296600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This part of the story is supposed to have elements of a rom-com, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The LARP is a mixed template game so a certain amount of disbelief needs to occur to have any of these templates hang out in the same room as each other. The two werewolves in game aren't even a full pack yet and they are both pretty young and idealistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T08:04:18-07:00","id":297121,"title":"","content":"Two werewolves &amp; a mage? That's not a pack, it's the plot of WOD threesome porn.<br /> <br /> Or an Anita Blake novel, which is very similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T13:58:13-07:00","id":297485,"title":"","content":"&quot;Two girls, one mage.&quot; But in all seriousness, they aren't an official pack yet but soon another player will be joining as a Werewolf so they can finally get a group totem. The younger Werewolf <i>really</i> doesn't like my character and is intensely suspicious of my motives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T18:37:51-07:00","id":297690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=297485#post297485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Two girls, one mage.&quot; But in all seriousness, they aren't an official pack yet but soon another player will be joining as a Werewolf so they can finally get a group totem. The younger Werewolf <i>really</i> doesn't like my character and is intensely suspicious of my motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paranoia is a healthy trait in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:13:13-07:00","id":297996,"title":"","content":"Dammit, I'm getting wrapped up in this story.<br /> <br /> It's telling that I'm interested in what's essentially a WoD soap opera. Interested and eagerly anticipating further detail. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T08:17:48-07:00","id":298156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=297996#post297996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit, I'm getting wrapped up in this story.<br /> <br /> It's telling that I'm interested in what's essentially a WoD soap opera. Interested and eagerly anticipating further detail. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hero's comment makes me happy. Also the player for the Werewolf Alpha PC is now aware of this thread and loves it.<br /> <br /> Update: More soap opera drama soon to come! This will be the most drama the star crossed PCs have faced to date!<br /> <br /> The Werewolf PC told my character, in a really heartfelt fashion, that she is concerned about my character's well being. They got a lot closer after a three night romantic getaway to Italy and she is concerned that my character's liver might someday fail if he continues his <i>excessive</i> level of drinking. This puts Prognos (my mage PC) in an awkward situation. Before she decides to get any more attached to him, Prognos needs to come clean and tell her:<br /> <br /> &quot;My liver is nothing to worry about because my hunter work is going to kill me long before the alcohol gets a chance to do the same. It is very rare that people in my line of work get to retire because of old age or injury, and considering the 'work load' I take on, I'm not going to be one of the lucky ones. Despite all my skill, cunning, and magic, one day I'm either going to get sloppy or run into something way too big for me to handle. When that day comes, I won't be coming home.&quot;<br /> <br /> P.S. One of the players recently asked our ST if he's enjoying running a WoD soap opera rather than the usual WoD game that centers around serious political intrigue. His response, &quot;Soap opera is sooooo much more fun!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","user":"Cardran","date":". 10-31-2014, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T08:52:57-07:00","id":298185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=297996#post297996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit, I'm getting wrapped up in this story.<br /> <br /> It's telling that I'm interested in what's essentially a WoD soap opera. Interested and eagerly anticipating further detail. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>90% of the supernatural shows on TV are one of these. From Dark Shadows and Buffy to Vampire Diaries and True Blood.<br /> <br /> We don't always like to admit it, but this is one of the things that brings us back every week, THE DRAMA!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T09:30:52-07:00","id":298249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=298185#post298185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't always like to admit it, but this is one of the things that brings us back every week, THE DRAMA!</div> </div> </div> </div>My darling carnivorous rage monster,<br /> I understand that I am merely a Mage and you are an apex killing machine, yet I feel that Fate (conveniently produced by my Archmaster Acanthus friend) has brought us together. While I know I shall never be worthy of you, if you could find some place in your cold, murdering heart a place for me, I shall prove myself worthy of your dominance.<br /> <br /> Hugs and kisses...Prognos.<br /> <br /> AAAAAAND....SEND!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T10:57:18-07:00","id":298294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=298249#post298249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My darling carnivorous rage monster,<br /> I understand that I am merely a Mage and you are an apex killing machine, yet I feel that Fate (conveniently produced by my Archmaster Acanthus friend) has brought us together. While I know I shall never be worthy of you, if you could find some place in your cold, murdering heart a place for me, I shall prove myself worthy of your dominance.<br /> <br /> Hugs and kisses...Prognos.<br /> <br /> AAAAAAND....SEND!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using that somewhere.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I'm curious why the mage has death as such a huge crutch. I realize the reality is that, as a hunter, he's likely to die, and I'm glad he embraces that, but a little part of me wonders if he's more afraid of living than anything else. Does he think that living with the consequences is really that much worse?<br /> <br /> Does he think death is preferable to the consequences of investing in the wolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-31-2014, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T11:30:43-07:00","id":298316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=298294#post298294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm curious why the mage has death as such a huge crutch. I realize the reality is that, as a hunter, he's likely to die, and I'm glad he embraces that, but a little part of me wonders if he's more afraid of living than anything else. Does he think that living with the consequences is really that much worse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Survivor's guilt can take you there quite easily. Faced with the unavoidable realization that you're going to die in the battlefield may free you, may let you fight so that some of your brothers in arms get back from that hell-hole... but then, you don't. And your friends went and died anyway. And you're left thinking &quot;... it should have been me... He had a daughter. He had fiancee. It should have been me...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T11:32:23-07:00","id":298317,"title":"","content":"It's a fair possibility. I'm just wondering what the specific story is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T12:49:34-07:00","id":298372,"title":"","content":"On the note of the drama, the games I run tend to look a little like this, going from romantic sub plots to action movie intensity. I eat this stuff up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T14:48:29-07:00","id":299309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=298294#post298294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious why the mage has death as such a huge crutch. I realize the reality is that, as a hunter, he's likely to die, and I'm glad he embraces that, but a little part of me wonders if he's more afraid of living than anything else. Does he think that living with the consequences is really that much worse?<br /> <br /> Does he think death is preferable to the consequences of investing in the wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their relationship has rapidly progressed to a point that he feels guilty that she cares so much about him considering he could be killed in a hunt at any point and it appears to be a relative certainty that one day this will be his fate. He didn't see it as fair to continue letting her get attached to him without warning her of the potential heartbreak of his untimely demise. She didn't want to end the relationship though so instead he promised to let her help him research for his hunts and he will no longer drink while &quot;on the job.&quot; <br /> <br /> She tried to argue that she should go with him on hunts to keep him safe but that was quickly shot down by my character because we both know she is no good in combat situations [Has almost no combat experience in her back story or in game and her strength+brawl is so bad that even in Gauru form she only has 3 attack dice <i>before</i> penalty modifiers]. She grudgingly accepted that outcome but made me promise to be careful. She wants to spend a lot more time with my character. <br /> <br /> Next anticipated problem: Apparently the other Werewolf in her pack has written a back story where, (1) her biological family are pure and she doesn't know it, and (2) apparently a hunter from my compact was responsible for killing her mother. This is not the Werewolf my PC is dating, rather it is her younger werewolf ward. Eventually, I'm going to have to deal with making sure that the pure pack doesn't murder my PC's Forsaken girlfriend in order to recover their offspring and I'm also going to have to resolve the issue of being affiliated with someone that committed matricide against the younger wolf. The player who owns the younger wolf PC delights in creating drama for this rom-com that's occurred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T19:54:44-07:00","id":299547,"title":"","content":"In a rom-com scenario I can almost imagine the following scenario should Prognos and his Uratha girlfriend break up<br /> <br /> <b>Scene:</b> Inside a Bar<br /> <br /> Here we see Prognos sitting at a bar, stacks of empty beer cans are arranged in a pyramid in front of him. His best friend, let us name him Jake is by his side trying to console him<br /> <br /> <b>Prognos:</b> &quot;I knew a woman once, finest woman I ever knew. Why, with the arch of a single eyebrow, she claimed she could level an entire city.&quot;<br /> <b>Jake:</b> &quot;So why didn't she do that?&quot;<br /> <b>Prognos:</b> &quot;She liked to have a good bath every so often&quot;<br /> <br /> Cue laugh track","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T21:27:52-07:00","id":299663,"title":"","content":"Nice to see him taking steps, but the likelihood of him dying is still being used as an excuse.<br /> <br /> I'm rooting for them to really get to trusting each other and trusting each other and really living as a result of that, that way they can die in a blaze of glory together or to old age together.<br /> <br /> Of course, if I was Gming this, I would also be throwing everything I could to make that not happen. Die desperate and alone.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, this upcoming packmate problem looks to be a biggy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T11:06:00-08:00","id":300210,"title":"","content":"Oh it is totally an excuse. The events surrounding his Awakening have to this day left him a guilt and fear stricken mess that dives into hunter work so he can tell himself that he isn't turning into a monster like his mentor. The werewolf is actually the much more reasonable one in this pairing (except for the odd occasion when she goes alpha wolf on their relationship problems).<br /> <br /> Prognos isn't all bad though, he volunteered to do a favor for the Hierarch so he could take Tasha (the werewolf alpha) to Italy, was very understanding when it looked like they might have to break up to placate Tasha's unruly ward, and is even going to do a supernal pact just to give up alcohol as a present to Tasha. He treats her rather well, he treats himself like crap. Now the latter trend might eventually have a negative effect on the former trend, but hey: that's plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","user":"Cardran","date":". 11-02-2014, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T11:51:33-08:00","id":303559,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post, but I hadn't updated this versus interesting new events. Seeing as Prognos's opinion of werewolves has been substantially softened he is going to be attempting to help Tasha's two wolf pack contain and restrain an upcoming Rahu's first change. Although Prognos hates the idea of having to use non-lethal methods to try and stop a Death Raging apex werewolf, the werewolves have managed to get this surly Hunter to agree to more passive methods of capture and promise that the silver will only come out if there is no other way to stop the Rahu from killing an innocent person (to be more convincing about this promise he swore to it via a Fate 2 oath).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:21:42-08:00","id":303914,"title":"","content":"I am assuming you are an Acanthus with at least 4 dots in your primary arcana being that you mentioned early on using a 4 dot shield. If that is the case, if you have Fate 2+, just use Evil Eye to destroy his rolls. If you are Time 4, use Present as Past or Chronos' Curse to make life stupidly easy for restraint. Hell, you could use Acceleration to make yourself practically untouchable to a brand new Uratha anyway regardless of if they are Rahu or not. With proper shielding + acceleration, you are looking at a minimum of 8 defense.<br /> <br /> Pair that with a decreased defense on his part and you should come out looking like Adonis and Hercules combined in front of your girlfriend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:58:11-08:00","id":304969,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I actually talked with the ST and the other players about this and I'm purposefully pulling some of my punches because part of the player fun for this encounter is that it should be scary. That's just not going to happen if I set it up so the Rahu is <i>convinced</i> that a giant gargoyle is fighting them in melee (hanging time spell of extended cast Hallucination) while imposing on them a -16 to attack anyone in the group as long as I spend mana each turn. <br /> <br /> Besides, Prognos doesn't need to impress her any further in terms of combat prowess. Neither of the two current werewolves are very well statted for combat so when they played a &quot;pouncing lesson&quot; game with him the other night in Urhan form, the results were interesting. After collectively failing to get him after roughly a dozen chance die throws and repeatedly tying them up with well thrown bolas, Prognos used Gain Skill: Brawl on himself and managed to pin his girlfiend's wolf form. She acted annoyed at the time but when they returned to her place my PC was rewarded with some exciting time behind closed bedroom doors. He's lucky that he's dating a werewolf that falls much more on the human end of the werewolf spectrum; with most other werewolves, I likely would have had my throat slit later that night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T17:58:22-08:00","id":307034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=304969#post304969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I actually talked with the ST and the other players about this and I'm purposefully pulling some of my punches because part of the player fun for this encounter is that it should be scary</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with that to a point. The first change usually results in bad shit happening mostly because they were not noticed early enough and hence the unrestricted rampage. If he is a Rahu, it almost might do him good to become stronger if during the night of his first change, he was basically put in his place. Uratha need to learn to control their rage, especially a Rahu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T09:44:30-08:00","id":407846,"title":"","content":"I resurrected this thread because I wanted to give the final summary of what happened with this rom-com plot. Eventually the mage and werewolf fell deeply in love with one another despite near constant arguments and shouting matches between the two characters (symptom of their relative personalities). Prognos, my Mage/Hunter character, eventually became so emotionally attached to his lover that he began acting protective towards her entire pack (they aren't a very high combat statted pack and he was a <i>very</i> well combat statted gun mage). At one point, Prognos even found out that Tasha's werewolf cousin was being hold captive by a pack halfway across the world and managed to rescue the young Uratha before his lover even knew that she was in danger.<br /> <br /> Then some out of game considerations required me to get rid of my character, so we needed to plan out a death scene. A literal horde of Beshilu, led by a very powerful and intelligent rat king, was feeling threatened after they had been discovered by Tasha's pack. These Beshilu feared that the pack would pull more werewolves into the territory where this &quot;rat empire&quot; (the ST actually described it as such) has been living happily for around 100 years; so, naturally, they decided to try to assassinate the pack with increasingly aggressive tactics (including suicide bombers). The rat king used some beshilu power that lets him see the future and discovered that his greatest threat was from my time mage PC so he set up a causality trap wherein everything my character tried to do to stop the Beshilu's attacks resulted in either Prognos or Tasha dying.<br /> <br /> Sacrificing himself in a blaze of glory, Prognos used a mastery level creative thaumaturgy that is self damaging as part of its limiting factors and cast it on a scale that allowed him to wipe out massive numbers of Beshilu at the cost of his own body and soul. Tasha narrowly avoided going into Death Rage as she tearfully said her goodbyes to the dying mage. In his will, he left her a Celtic cross pendant which was the last gift he had received from his dead parents and had it enchanted to grant her mage armor and mental shielding. He also left her his 1964 black Chevy Impala (yes, the car IS a reference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), along with a letter that materialized out of time itself, which explained that he knew he was going to die before it happened, that Time magic told him that it was inevitable that one of them was going to die, and he gladly decided to give up his life for the safety of her pack.<br /> <br /> This is all hilariously juxtaposed by the fact that my replacement PC is an arrogant, rude, Silver Ladder, 16 year old, Spirit mage that likes to play pranks via Fate magic, makes Roused Spirit fetishes (so it appears that he has a spirit contained within a fetish, which is ALSO a spirit...), and purposefully spirit urges himself as a precaution against hostile mental effects. Needless to say, Tasha is far less friendly towards this new character; he is a constant annoyance to her Alpha Forsaken sensibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","user":"Cardran","date":". 02-17-2015, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T15:07:36-08:00","id":408231,"title":"","content":"You're breaking my heart with that ending, man.<br /> <br /> Also I hate your replacement PC. Probably not as much as Tasha does, though.<br /> <br /> Let me just say that this is the first time I have read this thread, and it was wonderful. Thank you for sharing this with us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T10:45:52-08:00","id":409092,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you enjoyed reading it. I enjoyed playing it. It's kind of a drag that I had to kill off the character for confidential out of character reasons, because the soap opera that made up this mismatched relationship created so many feels for everyone involved regardless of whether they were arguing, belligerent, flirting, or sweet. Since you, and a few other people from the original posting of this thread, all seemed to enjoy hearing about the story, I'll give you a bit more information about what is going on with it. <br /> <br /> In the aftermath of Prognos's death, the following occurred:<br /> <br /> 1. Prognos set it up so a Guardian of the Veil that owed him a life debt would Sanctify a fate oath on the mage PC that will be replacing my dead character as the most powerful PC in the game. The mage PC needed to promise he will aid Tasha's pack unquestioningly when his help is requested (pursuant to a few stipulations relating to morally problematic situations), or that PC would not receive his item from Prognos's will (a watch that imparts permanent Shield of Chronos and Mental Shield, cast on an AOE around the item that Fate exempts all people except the wearer). He did this to make sure that some powerful mage would be protecting Tasha in his absence.<br /> <br /> 2. The werewolf adoptive little sister of Tasha, a 19 year old college student that is extremely naiive and has a tendency to stick her nose into trouble, was in denial for a while about Prognos's death. She had grown pretty close to him over the course of her Alpha's romantic relationship with the mage and although she originally thought Prognos was going to go full, silver wielding, Hunter on their pack, she eventually came to see him as an honorary member of the pack and thus a part of her family. This young wolf, Fen, doesn't handle death of loved ones very well and that combined with the fact that she believed Prognos to be too powerful to be killed by anything led Fen to believe that Prognos faked his own death and is &quot;obviously&quot; still alive. This eventually led to a full on pack brawl when Tasha attacked Fen in Urshul while demanding that Fen accept the fact that Prognos is, in fact, dead. <br /> <br /> 3. Tasha's first act upon getting home the day of Prognos's death was to violently smash everything on the first floor of her pack's home except for the sofa that their Bear totem likes to sleep on. She doesn't let anyone else touch the impala she inherited from him and wears the pendant at all times. Largely using Prognos's own flask, she was originally delving into her dead lover's self destructive method of coping with life: excessive alcoholism. Two young mages that Prognos had awakened and spent time with regularly to help them get acclimated to their new lives decided to step in and prevent Tasha's alcoholism, as a favor to their dead friend, and managed to get a Supernal Wraith to transfer over to Tasha the anti-alcohol ban that was originally imposed on Prognos up until minutes before he died (ingesting alcohol of any kind will cause lethal damage and become supernaturally addictive). Tasha is currently counting down the days until she can once again drink her woes away and in the mean time she is having a mind/life mage regularly alter her brain's neural receptors to artificially produce more dopamine. She's become much more snappish with all the other characters and has little patience for other people, including her own pack members at times. She is considering going bar hoping while regularly Skin Changed and picking up one night stands to cope with the grief (knowing how strong her libido is, Prognos's final letter encouraged her to do so if she is so inclined :P).<br /> <br /> 4. We may run a plot with her going on an astral journey with the help of a mind mage so she can try to enter her own Werewolf version of the Oneiros and confront the various personal demons plaguing her...including those related to Prognos's death. If we decide to go that route (the main ST may decline to allow it), I will get to write that out as an assistant ST and I am going to make it soooooooo traumatic. If she decides to flee from the Oneiros challenges her mental state in the physical world will get much, much worse and at that point the <i>only</i> way to recover from her grief will be to go back into her Oneiros and succeed in overcoming her issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=408231#post408231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> . . . I hate your replacement PC. Probably not as much as Tasha does, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, what is it about the replacement that you hate so much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:10:52-08:00","id":409135,"title":"","content":"I'm engaging in hyperbole with regard to the replacement PC, actually. This is more a 'but he'll never be as great as the guy he's replacing' ... because his life isn't such a sitcom,<br /> <br /> As for the rest of events, wow, you people managed to make the aftermath wonderfully dramatic in its own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:46:12-08:00","id":409188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/287798-on-odd-rp-question?p=409135#post409135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm engaging in hyperbole with regard to the replacement PC, actually. This is more a 'but he'll never be as great as the guy he's replacing' ... because his life isn't such a sitcom,<br /> <br /> As for the rest of events, wow, you people managed to make the aftermath wonderfully dramatic in its own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah that makes sense, and, sadly, I agree :'(. <br /> <br /> As for the aftermath, yeah our game is kind of outside the norm for the mood and theme of most nWoD games. Rather than making the central focus on horrifying mysteries and political games of life/death (although we still make the horror show up on a decently regular basis), we have soap opera, whacky star-trek esque space adventures, challenging the stereotypes of the various templates (e.g. high harmony Predator King pack), and some pretty unexpected humor (Strix obsessed with comedy, harvest festival spirit drinking parties, changeling run ice cream shops, zombified roast rabbits that serve themselves for dinner, etc.). <br /> <br /> The werewolf players in particular actively seek out in game drama as much as possible so I expect much more heartache stories to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}